  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A notice board and the member contact list can carry the same dated update; brief acknowledgment does not require agreement with the change.\", \"decision\": \"How should members receive changes to studio routines?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe steward explains each dated update at members’ next arrivals and points them to the notice board. The explanation occurs where the changed routine will be used and allows immediate questions about its practical effect.\nMembers read dated updates on the notice board and mark an acknowledgment beside their names before starting work. The steward can identify who still needs an explanation without repeating the update to every arriving member.\nThe steward sends each dated update through the contact list and posts it on the notice board before it takes effect. Members can prepare before arriving and find the same instructions inside the studio."
    }
  ],
